rt apps must be deployed on unique, isolated cores, and should go into pending if there's not enough cores

{color:#000000}*Summary:*{color}

{color:#000000}Due to the removal of PHC3 from the project, the hosted segments will need to be deployed within the MES PaaS RT Region. There a need to support pinning applications to an isolated core dynamically in this environment. Our goal is to prototype the usage of native kubernetes capabilities to handle this dynamization.{color}

*Project Impact:*
{color:#000000}What Problem Does this Solve{color}
 * Aligns with future state of project
 * Supports dynamic deployments of applications with available cores in the MES PaaS application. 

{color:#000000}How does this fit into the larger project{color}
 * Following the PHC3-MES PaaS consolidation the hosted segment applications such as TCAP and ESTAP controller will be deployed to MES. Prototyping the usage of Control CPU Management Policies on the Node supports the use of RT on the MES PaaS RT Region.

{color:#000000}*Implementation Overview:*{color}
{color:#000000}High Level Overview{color}
 * {color:#000000}Investigate Control CPU Management Policies on a Node in the RKE2 docs. {color}

 * {color:#000000}Manually update a TBD server (or use a vm) to use static CPU management policy.{color}

 * {color:#000000}Update helm charts in a way that ensures a dummy rt application is pinned to an isolated core. {color}

{color:#000000}Key Components/Docs{color}
 * [https://kubernetes.io/docs/tasks/administer-cluster/cpu-management-policies/]
 * [https://kubernetes.io/blog/2024/12/16/cpumanager-strict-cpu-reservation/] 

{color:#000000}*Risks/Considerations/Dependencies*{color}
 * {color:#000000}The CPU management policy may not work in a way that supports our use case. {color}
 * {color:#000000}RKE2 may change applications core affinity while the application is running.{color}

{color:#000000}*Completion Criteria:*{color}

{color:#000000}Specs{color}
 * {color:#000000}Confluence page containing the process to set up the static CPU configuration policy and the end result of the prototyped effort{color}

{color:#000000}Outputs{color}
 * {color:#000000}Example RT application helm charts which contains configuration that results in application being pinned on a node.{color}

{color:#000000}*Summary:*{color}

{color:#000000}Due to the removal of PHC3 from the project, the hosted segments will need to be deployed within the MES PaaS RT Region. To ensure that CPU Affinity-based requirements are fulfilled via the RT region of the MES cluster, there is a need to define / create tests. This milestone will cover the design and implementation of an MVP RT test tool and will be shared amongst LM and GDEB for consistent RT testing.  {color}

*Project Impact:*
{color:#000000}What Problem Does this Solve{color}
 * Aligns with future state of project
 * Supports continuing integration of rt applications with MES PaaS. 

{color:#000000}How does this fit into the larger project{color}
 * Supports the continual integration of rt applications with MES PaaS. 
 * Shared tool between LM and EB for uniform and comparable results. 

{color:#000000}*Implementation Overview:*{color}
{color:#000000}High Level Overview{color}
 * {color:#000000}Investigate various tests that can be used to verify both RT configuration and performance. {color}
 * {color:#000000}The MVP test tool will determine which cores are isolated on a server dynamically and will verify that the application is appropriately pinned to a core when scheduling new applications. {color}

{color:#000000}Key Components/Docs{color}
 * TBD Confluence Page
 * Background Context: [https://192.168.3.34/cnfl1/display/DS/RT+Scheduler]

{color:#000000}*Risks/Considerations/Dependencies*{color}
 * {color:#000000}Lack of knowledge{color}

{color:#000000}*Completion Criteria:*{color}

{color:#000000}Specs{color}
 * {color:#000000}A detailed confluence page listing out the RT tests {color}

{color:#000000}Outputs{color}
 * {color:#000000}An MVP RT test applications that has the distinct purpose of verifying an RT application when deployed in kubernetes is running on a isolated core.  {color}
 * CI/CD pipeline job in TBD repo that shows the test app reporting "success" for an RT application running on isolated core and "failure" when RT app is running on non-isolated core.

